A canvas under a `for` hands its handler the host event, as a slot child does.

passCanvasInstances makes such a canvas an instance and its handlers the
instance's events. It lifted them by hand with a relay that emitted nothing
and an event that declared no parameters, so `@click(e)` got an `e` nothing
passed. It now lifts through the slot-child lifting, whose relay takes the
host event and emits it.

html only: fyne and gtk4 wire no canvas click at all, and a handler naming
its `ClickEvent` names a type neither emits.

deny out/none/html/index.html `__prop___on0\(\)` -- the relay passes the host event on
-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import draw "sngl:ui/draw"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
}

component main node {
    var hits = 0
    var xs = [1, 2]

    vbox {
        text(value="hits {hits}")
        for var x = xs {
            draw.canvas(width=40px, height=40px, @click(e) { hits += x }) {
                draw.circle(cx=20.0, cy=20.0, r=float(x) * 5.0)
            }
        }
    }
}

window {
    main
}
